# Base surface color

When building any new creation surface — tables, panels, cards, editors,
overlays, etc. — use the same base background as documents:

```
var(--surface-base)
```

| Theme | `--surface-base` | `--text-primary` |
|---|---|---|
| Dark (default) | `#151515` | `#fff` |
| Light (`data-theme="light"`) | `#F1F1F1` | `#3D3B3B` |

## Rules

- Default base/fill for new surfaces = `var(--surface-base)` (not a hardcoded hex).
- Default body/UI text on those surfaces = `var(--text-primary)` or `var(--text)`.
- Keep this consistent so new UI reads as part of the same document system.
- Fullscreen overlays that must stay dark (URL table, export pack/workspace, i/e chooser, confirm) keep `#151515` / white text — pin `--surface-base: #151515` on the overlay root.
- Only deviate when the user explicitly asks for a different color.
